{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And I will turn toward you</b> — פני (My face) [has the numerical value of] ת\"י (410), [corresponding to] the two times [totaling] 420 years that the Temple stood; My face was there, as written: \"My eyes and My heart shall be there all the days\"; but after they were exiled — \"where has your beloved turned?\""], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The gematria פני = ת\"י = 410 is stated; the phrase שת\"י שנים (\"two [times] 420 years\") refers to the combined standing-time of both Temples, which the Ba'al HaTurim apparently reads as 420 (First Temple 410 + Second Temple 10, by a known rabbinic reckoning). The closing phrase quotes Song of Songs 5:17 (Eng. 5:6), שאנה פנה דודך, applied as a wordplay on פניתי/פני."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:45.712171375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}